WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.250
Attackers sat inside at least

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:03.905
three AI hosts for weeks,

00:00:03.705 --> 00:00:05.489
copying customer prompts.

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:07.810
Nobody noticed until a researcher

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.365
told them.

00:00:09.065 --> 00:00:10.907
On Sunday, OpenRouter,

00:00:10.707 --> 00:00:12.207
a big model router,

00:00:12.007 --> 00:00:14.260
dropped three providers and pulled

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.518
one hundred twenty-five endpoints from

00:00:16.318 --> 00:00:17.682
zero data retention.

00:00:18.232 --> 00:00:20.073
Dragos sent about two million

00:00:19.873 --> 00:00:21.713
prompts with unique fake keys

00:00:21.513 --> 00:00:22.239
and links.

00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:23.741
Each secret went to one

00:00:23.541 --> 00:00:25.270
place, so any hit exposed

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:25.736
the leak.

00:00:26.286 --> 00:00:27.850
At least three hosts had

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.828
attackers inside, from mid July.

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:32.176
They used a couple hundred

00:00:31.976 --> 00:00:33.826
bait AWS keys for tens

00:00:33.626 --> 00:00:35.751
of thousands of API calls.

00:00:36.301 --> 00:00:37.823
Others needed no hack.

00:00:37.863 --> 00:00:40.569
Marketplace sellers logged requests,

00:00:40.369 --> 00:00:43.289
some services forwarded traffic quietly,

00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:44.864
and one Chinese lab opened

00:00:44.664 --> 00:00:46.654
links in over half its prompts.

00:00:47.204 --> 00:00:48.692
Three hosts have explained.

00:00:48.732 --> 00:00:50.319
An attacker got into Phala

00:00:50.119 --> 00:00:51.517
through an old service.

00:00:51.557 --> 00:00:52.813
At Together AI,

00:00:52.613 --> 00:00:54.995
a coding agent leaked a credential.

00:00:55.035 --> 00:00:57.538
Novita misrouted MiniMax requests.

00:00:58.088 --> 00:01:00.172
Zero data retention should stop

00:00:59.972 --> 00:01:01.498
hosts storing prompts.

00:01:01.538 --> 00:01:02.889
Some ignored it,

00:01:02.689 --> 00:01:05.334
attackers inside read requests live,

00:01:05.134 --> 00:01:06.557
and it binds only the

00:01:06.357 --> 00:01:07.420
first company.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.957
Rotate any secret sent through

00:01:09.757 --> 00:01:11.263
a router or small host

00:01:11.063 --> 00:01:11.813
since May.

00:01:11.853 --> 00:01:14.408
Give agents short-lived credentials,

00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:16.070
and plant fake keys as alarms.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.683
Cheap tokens were always paid

00:01:18.483 --> 00:01:19.429
for somehow.

00:01:19.469 --> 00:01:20.920
For some, the price was

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:21.635
their prompts.

00:01:21.675 --> 00:01:23.444
Full story on The Dispatch.

